Status: Force rebuild — snapshot pipeline fixes (3 in 1)
Audit found: 0 snapshot notifications in DB across all time, despite
worker running and INTERNAL_SYNC_TOKEN being set. Root cause: the
send-snapshot endpoint read its token via process.env.INTERNAL_SYNC_TOKEN
while the sync endpoint uses env from $env/dynamic/private. SvelteKit's
adapter-node may inline process.env.X to undefined at build time when
the var isn't visible to Vite — silently breaking the worker's calls
and producing 401s the worker logged but no notifications.
Three fixes shipped:
  1. send-snapshot now reads INTERNAL_SYNC_TOKEN via $env/dynamic/private
     (runtime read, matches sync endpoint).
  2. Endpoint logs structured JSON on every call (actor=worker|user, kind,
     sent/deduped/errors counts, elapsed_ms) so future failures are visible.
  3. Page header status panel: "Snapshots (30d): ☀ N morning · last X · 🌙
     N evening · last Y · ✉ N manual · last Z" — or amber "never fired"
     warning when zero. Reads notifications.source_id history via SPLIT_PART.
